ation to really smash  it you know smash it like the hulk if  you will  is to um start somewhere to start  somewhere anywhere  and this employs actually a rule in  psychology called the zeigarnik effect  the zygarnic effect basically this  psychiatrist or psychologist  in europe was noticing that when she was  out at the cafe  that the the wait staff was never taking  writing down her orders  and at all and you ever had a waiter  waitress like that you go to dinner and  they take like five or six  when i waitress that was me it's amazing  and then i was as a kid i was wondering  how do they do that because i remember  for me it was like a big belief change  but i knew it was really possible and  what they're executing in if they don't  have an actual strategy for it like i'm  like one of the memory techniques we  teach  um is the zeigarnik effect and basically  what she found when she was researching  it is they would hold that order in  their mind but as soon as they delivered  it the order would disappear  right you know because it was close they  got closure and the zygarde  effect is basically saying your brain  doesn't like open loops  open loops meaning you start something  but don't finish it right it doesn't  like that dissonance um and so it needs  closure  right um like a kiss good night kind of  thing and so what was happening here is  that  they were remembering the orders and  they would hold on to it  until they actually was um delivered and  then  that's the zygarnic effect and so the  idea here is start something  and you'll be you have this impulse to  finish it and you know until it's done  right but you start somewhere as opposed  to not starting anything  and then the last tip i would give  people to overcome procrastination so  you could hit your top three things  today  is to be kind to yourself to be kind to  yourself  because you would think that people  intuitively beat themselves up  over procrastinating you know i didn't  get my i didn't g